>    I recently started a game as a Barbarian, and in the room I started
>in, I found a Longsword named Demonblade.  Out of the hundreds of times
>I've played this game, it was the first time I EVER found a sword with a
>name. Is there a trick to finding a special sword? What levels are more
>likely to have them? And what swords are there? (I've seen Demonblade,
>and heard of Frost Brand on this newsgroup.)

You are very unlikely to find a named weapon just laying around.  I
think in all the games I've played, I've only found a named weapon
maybe two or three times.  The two most common ways to get a named
weapon are these:

	1)  Wish for it.  To do this properly, you must give the
		proper weapon type.  You could wish for a bullwhip
		named Demonbane, but it would just be a plain old
		bullwhip with a fancy name, unlike the long sword.

	2)  Get your deity to give it to you.  If you #offer enough
		sacrifices, your deity will give you a named weapon.
		He will only give out certain ones, however.  Don't
		expect a Chaotic deity to reward you with Excalibur.

There are other, easier ways to get Excalibur and less powerful named
weapons, but they are beyond the scope of this post.

